---
/**
 * Lamplight's privacy policy (the Android game). Linked from Google Play and from the game's Settings.
 * Facts come from the build: progress is saved only on the device; the game itself makes no network
 * requests; the only third party is the Google Mobile Ads SDK, which shows optional rewarded videos
 * requested as child-directed (no advertising ID, no personalised ads, content rating G).
 * If the build changes (analytics, purchases, accounts, another SDK), this page must change first.
 */
import LegalLayout from '../../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../../lib/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'who', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'summary', label: 'In short' },
  { id: 'device', label: 'Saved on your device' },
  { id: 'ads', label: 'Optional video ads' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'permissions', label: 'Permissions' },
  { id: 'delete', label: 'Deleting your data' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Lamplight privacy policy"
  description="How the Lamplight puzzle game for Android handles data: progress stays on your phone, no accounts, no analytics, and optional child-safe video ads from Google AdMob."
  updated="21 November 2026"
  toc={toc}
  crumbs={[
    { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
    { href: '/games', label: 'Games' },
    { href: '/games/lamplight', label: 'Lamplight' },
    { label: 'Privacy policy' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    This policy covers <strong>Lamplight</strong>, our puzzle game for Android (Google Play package
    <code>com.ismailapps.lamplight</code>). It explains what data the game handles, why, and what you can do about it. The
    website has its own <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Lamplight is made by IsmailApps, the name under which {site.founder.legalName} publishes software and games. It is not a
    registered company yet. The person responsible for your data (the controller) is:
  </p>
  <address>
    {site.founder.legalName}<br />
    {site.founder.postalAddress}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
  </address>

  <h2 id="summary">In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There are <strong>no accounts</strong>, no sign-in, no chat and no way to share personal information in the game.</li>
    <li>Your progress is saved <strong>only on your phone</strong>. We never receive it.</li>
    <li>We use <strong>no analytics and no tracking</strong>, and the game sells nothing for real money.</li>
    <li>
      The only outside service is <strong>Google AdMob</strong>, for video ads you choose to watch. Ads are requested as
      directed to children: no advertising ID, no personalised ads.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="device">Saved on your device</h2>
  <p>
    The game keeps a save file on your phone with your progress: streets lit, stars, coins, hearts, hints, daily challenge
    results, your day streak, how many videos you watched today (each reward has a daily limit), a few times and dates (so
    hearts can refill while the game is closed), and your settings (sound, music, vibration, reduced motion). It stays in the game's private storage on your device. We
    have no server for it, and the game does not send it anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ads">Optional video ads (Google AdMob)</h2>
  <p>
    Some rewards, such as a free heart, a hint or extra coins, come from a short video ad that you choose to start with a
    "Watch Video" button. Ads never appear on their own and never during a puzzle. The game works fully without watching any.
  </p>
  <p>
    The videos are provided by Google's Mobile Ads SDK (Google AdMob). Every ad request from Lamplight is marked as
    <strong>directed to children and under the age of consent</strong>, with the content rating limited to
    <strong>G</strong> (general audiences). With this setting, Google does not send the device's advertising ID and does
    not show personalised ads or remarketing.
  </p>
  <p>
    To show an ad, count it and prevent fraud, the Google Mobile Ads SDK still processes some technical information. Google
    lists this as: the device's IP address (which can indicate a rough location), other device and app identifiers (such as
    the app set ID), how you interact with ads, and diagnostic information such as crashes and performance. It is encrypted
    in transit. Google handles this information under its own policies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from apps that use its services</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure" rel="noopener">What the Google Mobile Ads SDK collects</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not receive any of this information about you. We only see totals in our AdMob account, such as how many videos
    were shown.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Legal basis:</strong> showing optional, non-personalised ads to fund a free game is our legitimate interest (Art.
    6(1)(f) GDPR). You can avoid all ad processing by never tapping "Watch Video".
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    Lamplight is made for all ages. We do not ask for, and do not knowingly collect, personal information from anyone,
    including children under 13. The ads are requested in Google's child-directed mode described above, which is designed
    for apps that children may use (including under the US COPPA rule). If you are a parent and have a question, email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="permissions">Permissions</h2>
  <p>
    Lamplight asks for no permissions that need your approval. Android grants it internet and network-state access, used
    only to load the optional videos, and vibration, for the small buzz when you turn a tile (you can turn this off in
    Settings). The Google Mobile Ads SDK also declares the advertising ID permission. Because every request is marked as
    child-directed, the ID is not sent.
  </p>

  <h2 id="delete">Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Uninstalling the game, or clearing its storage in Android's settings, deletes your progress from the phone. We have no
    copy, so it cannot be restored afterwards. You can reset your advertising ID or delete it in Android's settings
    (Settings › Privacy › Ads, or Settings › Google › Ads, depending on your phone).
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us about any personal data we hold about you, and ask us to correct or delete it. In practice we hold none
    from the game. For data processed by Google to show ads, Google's policy explains your choices. You can also complain to
    a data protection supervisory authority. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will reply
    within a month.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If the game starts handling data differently, for example a new feature or another service, we will update this page
    and the date at the top before that version is released.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
